1
00:01:28,284 --> 00:01:34,089
BATTLE FOR THE BONUS

2
00:01:35,924 --> 00:01:37,092
Well, everyone.

3
00:01:37,293 --> 00:01:41,930
For many years now, we have been troubled by one person in particular.

4
00:01:42,131 --> 00:01:43,065
That person is...

5
00:01:43,265 --> 00:01:44,233
this man!

6
00:01:47,770 --> 00:01:48,971
At this time each year,

7
00:01:49,171 --> 00:01:54,076
our successive leaders of the group have tried all sorts to take him down.

8
00:01:54,276 --> 00:01:55,110
But...

9
00:02:02,084 --> 00:02:06,522
Every attempt has ended in failure, leaving us with a heavy sense of defeat.

10
00:02:06,722 --> 00:02:08,524
They were just one step away.

11
00:02:08,724 --> 00:02:11,260
I still feel the humiliation of two years ago.

12
00:02:11,527 --> 00:02:15,397
I can't sleep at night because I'm so frustrated thinking about this man.

13
00:02:15,998 --> 00:02:17,499
Yes, yes.

14
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:20,102
But this year will be different.

15
00:02:20,302 --> 00:02:22,938
As our new leader, I'm going to make sure of it.

16
00:02:27,309 --> 00:02:31,280
This year, I'm going to collect the money Kankichi Ryotsu owes us!

17
00:02:35,551 --> 00:02:40,055
That's a very impressive introduction, but we need to get down to business now.

18
00:02:40,289 --> 00:02:41,690
I know.

19
00:02:42,558 --> 00:02:43,692
So, everyone.

20
00:02:44,059 --> 00:02:49,665
The strategy meeting for the 21st Battle for Kankichi Ryotsu's Bonus is in motion.

21
00:02:49,865 --> 00:02:53,769
There, there. It'll be over soon.

22
00:02:54,002 --> 00:02:59,742
Kikuchi-san, we can't have you bringing your baby to important meetings.

23
00:02:59,975 --> 00:03:01,210
What else can I do?

24
00:03:01,410 --> 00:03:05,447
My wife called me a good-for-nothing who can't even collect his debts!

25
00:03:05,681 --> 00:03:07,916
Then she moved out.

26
00:03:09,084 --> 00:03:14,189
Ryo-san's unpaid food delivery bills are getting taken out of my own salary.

27
00:03:14,556 --> 00:03:19,027
Still, I doubt any of our schemes will actually work against Ryo-san.

28
00:03:19,228 --> 00:03:20,896
What are you saying, you wimp!

29
00:03:21,096 --> 00:03:24,867
Your father-in-law, the previous manager of Sato Denki,

30
00:03:25,067 --> 00:03:27,403
was the eighth chair of the shopping district.

31
00:03:27,603 --> 00:03:30,639
He dedicated his life to collecting Ryo-san's debts!

32
00:03:30,873 --> 00:03:34,076
Yeah, Sukeroku-san was passionate about everything he did.

33
00:03:34,276 --> 00:03:37,212
He was the one who started the sports day too.

34
00:03:37,412 --> 00:03:39,915
But then he had to go and get a slipped disk.

35
00:03:40,282 --> 00:03:42,484
-Sorry, but that was hilarious. -It was.

36
00:03:45,187 --> 00:03:46,088
Ahem!

37
00:03:46,822 --> 00:03:51,927
So, this time, I've prepared a secret weapon to get my hands on Ryo-san's bonus.

38
00:03:52,127 --> 00:03:53,262
A secret weapon?

39
00:03:53,962 --> 00:03:58,066
I've acquired many skills from 30 years in the plastic model shop business,

40
00:03:58,267 --> 00:04:02,404
and I spent three months and 90% of our membership fees developing it.

41
00:04:06,208 --> 00:04:09,044
This is the Kankichi Ryotsu Navigation System.

42
00:04:09,244 --> 00:04:10,446
"Ryo Navi" for short.

43
00:04:10,779 --> 00:04:15,451
Everything is ready! Now we just catch Ryo-san on the day and take his bonus.

44
00:04:15,651 --> 00:04:16,418
Yeah!

45
00:04:16,618 --> 00:04:18,921
I call it "Operation Sky Eye!"

46
00:04:27,696 --> 00:04:30,632
Ryotsu-san. Kankichi Ryotsu from Community Affairs.

47
00:04:30,833 --> 00:04:31,500
Here!

48
00:04:31,967 --> 00:04:33,469
Here's your bonus.

49
00:04:33,669 --> 00:04:35,137
Yahoo!

50
00:04:37,139 --> 00:04:40,108
That's 182-and-a-half days of work and toil.

51
00:04:40,309 --> 00:04:43,445
Enduring the chief's sarcasm day after day,

52
00:04:43,645 --> 00:04:46,114
there was only one thing that kept me going...

53
00:04:48,817 --> 00:04:54,122
Oh! It was all for you, my beloved bonus!

54
00:04:54,323 --> 00:04:57,426
Ryo-san, what will you spend your bonus on this year?

55
00:04:58,293 --> 00:05:02,331
&lt;i&gt;I've already ordered a limited edition NASA radio-controlled space shuttle.&lt;/i&gt;

56
00:05:02,531 --> 00:05:05,434
&lt;i&gt;It's a 1/12th scale model.&lt;/i&gt;

57
00:05:05,634 --> 00:05:07,469
You always buy things like that.

58
00:05:07,669 --> 00:05:09,838
Well, I'm off to the bank.

59
00:05:10,038 --> 00:05:13,709
If I don't transfer the money today, the order will be cancelled.

60
00:05:27,022 --> 00:05:29,725
Dang, there's at least 30 of them.

61
00:05:29,925 --> 00:05:31,760
I need to be extra cautious today.

62
00:05:31,994 --> 00:05:33,028
Desperate times!

63
00:05:34,496 --> 00:05:35,230
He's late.

64
00:05:35,464 --> 00:05:37,299
He should be coming out now.

65
00:05:47,743 --> 00:05:50,345
Maybe he already left.

66
00:05:50,946 --> 00:05:55,784
&lt;i&gt;Heh... A pair of sunglasses is enough to have them fooled. Easy as pie.&lt;/i&gt;

67
00:05:57,085 --> 00:05:58,153
&lt;i&gt;Oh no, my bonus!&lt;/i&gt;

68
00:05:58,353 --> 00:06:00,889
Excuse me, ma'am.

69
00:06:01,089 --> 00:06:03,158
You dropped this.

70
00:06:03,926 --> 00:06:05,227
Oh, thank you very much.

71
00:06:05,427 --> 00:06:06,361
No, no.

72
00:06:06,895 --> 00:06:07,696
Eh?

73
00:06:08,196 --> 00:06:08,964
What is it?

74
00:06:09,197 --> 00:06:12,200
I thought for a second you were my runaway wife.

75
00:06:12,401 --> 00:06:15,203
But on closer inspection, you're much prettier.

76
00:06:15,704 --> 00:06:17,406
I'm honored. Well, goodbye.

77
00:06:17,606 --> 00:06:18,640
Take care.

78
00:06:19,207 --> 00:06:21,910
&lt;i&gt;That was close. But these guys must be blind.&lt;/i&gt;

79
00:06:22,110 --> 00:06:23,278
Hey, Ryo-san!

80
00:06:23,512 --> 00:06:24,179
What?

81
00:06:24,379 --> 00:06:25,781
You forgot your stamp.

82
00:06:26,248 --> 00:06:28,750
Oh, sorry! Uh-oh...

83
00:06:31,119 --> 00:06:32,387
Oh no!

84
00:06:32,588 --> 00:06:33,755
It's Ryo-san!

85
00:06:35,090 --> 00:06:36,658
Give me back my wife!

86
00:06:36,892 --> 00:06:37,993
And my salary!

87
00:06:38,226 --> 00:06:40,662
I knew this would happen...

88
00:06:40,896 --> 00:06:43,465
Take this! Exit, stage left!

89
00:06:48,303 --> 00:06:50,072
Hey! Not so fast!

90
00:06:50,272 --> 00:06:51,273
There he is!

91
00:06:54,543 --> 00:06:57,079
All right, time to take that bonus.

92
00:07:00,282 --> 00:07:02,818
-Kameda from the ramen shop? -Hey!

93
00:07:03,018 --> 00:07:05,087
-What's going on? -He's over there.

94
00:07:06,989 --> 00:07:07,823
But how?

95
00:07:08,023 --> 00:07:09,224
Damn it! He got away!

96
00:07:09,424 --> 00:07:11,293
Ozaki-san, please respond.

97
00:07:12,227 --> 00:07:13,562
&lt;i&gt;We're at the police HQ.&lt;/i&gt;

98
00:07:13,762 --> 00:07:16,598
&lt;i&gt;The ambush failed. Ryo-san has escaped.&lt;/i&gt;

99
00:07:16,798 --> 00:07:18,800
&lt;i&gt;Commence the operation immediately!&lt;/i&gt;

100
00:07:19,001 --> 00:07:19,801
Roger.

101
00:07:20,002 --> 00:07:22,004
Ozaki-san, is everything on track?

102
00:07:22,237 --> 00:07:25,273
I predicted that Ryo-san would escape at this stage.

103
00:07:25,474 --> 00:07:28,310
Now the real action starts with Operation Sky Eye!

104
00:07:29,611 --> 00:07:33,115
There's a navigation computer attached to Ryo-san's belt.

105
00:07:36,151 --> 00:07:38,587
A satellite picks up the signal,

106
00:07:38,787 --> 00:07:41,289
and lets us continually track his location.

107
00:07:42,257 --> 00:07:44,359
That's just gibberish to me.

108
00:07:44,593 --> 00:07:46,661
Will this really work?

109
00:07:46,862 --> 00:07:49,297
Even the US military uses this system here.

110
00:07:49,498 --> 00:07:51,800
It's over 200% reliable.

111
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,337
Well I don't trust new technology.

112
00:07:55,537 --> 00:07:58,707
Yes, well, this time you can just watch.

113
00:07:59,141 --> 00:08:00,709
Activating Ryo Navi!

114
00:08:08,483 --> 00:08:10,752
What's that flashing dot?

115
00:08:10,986 --> 00:08:12,387
That's his location.

116
00:08:14,056 --> 00:08:17,392
Target is heading toward Kameari General Bank via a back street.

117
00:08:17,726 --> 00:08:19,494
Get there first, and lie in wait.

118
00:08:19,695 --> 00:08:20,495
&lt;i&gt;Roger that.&lt;/i&gt;

119
00:08:20,695 --> 00:08:23,732
Ryo-san. No matter where you run, you can't escape us.

120
00:08:23,932 --> 00:08:27,235
We've got a bird's-eye view of your whereabouts.

121
00:08:27,769 --> 00:08:29,237
Yes, sorry!

122
00:08:29,938 --> 00:08:31,740
Yahoo! Huh?

123
00:08:32,207 --> 00:08:34,009
Welcome.

124
00:08:34,209 --> 00:08:35,510
We were waiting for you.

125
00:08:35,711 --> 00:08:38,480
Give your bonus to the Kameari shopping district.

126
00:08:38,914 --> 00:08:40,949
Oh no! They got here first!

127
00:08:46,388 --> 00:08:48,924
All right! Street Riders, move out!

128
00:08:50,959 --> 00:08:51,927
Go get him!

129
00:08:52,728 --> 00:08:54,329
Damn it.

130
00:08:55,130 --> 00:08:58,600
Time to show off the moped skills I honed through food deliveries!

131
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:01,603
They've got mopeds? In that case...

132
00:09:06,208 --> 00:09:06,808
What?

133
00:09:10,879 --> 00:09:12,380
Come back in ten years!

134
00:09:12,581 --> 00:09:13,348
Huh?

135
00:09:13,548 --> 00:09:16,818
You won't escape that easily. I was once a professional racer.

136
00:09:17,152 --> 00:09:20,255
Yeah, yeah. I could recite that story in my sleep!

137
00:09:20,455 --> 00:09:21,223
Take this!

138
00:09:29,631 --> 00:09:33,301
Hello... The Street Riders have been wiped out.

139
00:09:35,737 --> 00:09:38,940
He's heading to the next town across the Naka River.

140
00:09:39,141 --> 00:09:41,076
Ryo-san is heading to the next town.

141
00:09:41,276 --> 00:09:43,378
Cut him off on the bridge.

142
00:09:43,945 --> 00:09:47,382
Damn it... They're really going all out this year.

143
00:09:48,450 --> 00:09:53,321
It'll be safer to leave town and go to the bank in the next town.

144
00:09:53,555 --> 00:09:54,256
Huh?

145
00:09:58,126 --> 00:10:00,195
You're not getting through, Ryo-san.

146
00:10:00,595 --> 00:10:04,666
No! How did you know I was coming through here?

147
00:10:07,836 --> 00:10:09,838
Ryo-san. There's no way out.

148
00:10:10,038 --> 00:10:12,474
What the heck is going on?

149
00:10:13,508 --> 00:10:15,210
Hand over your bonus!

150
00:10:15,443 --> 00:10:17,846
Ryo-san, give us your bonus!

151
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:20,215
-Everyone... -Bonus, bonus...

152
00:10:20,615 --> 00:10:26,288
Bonus, bonus...

153
00:10:27,489 --> 00:10:30,525
No! You can't have it!

154
00:10:37,299 --> 00:10:40,769
To think he'd jump in the river in the middle of winter!

155
00:10:42,537 --> 00:10:44,172
Bah, he's getting away!

156
00:10:44,372 --> 00:10:45,607
Hold it right there!

157
00:10:45,807 --> 00:10:47,642
-Stop! Don't do it! -Let go of me!

158
00:10:47,843 --> 00:10:50,845
-It's cold in there. You'll die! -Get off! Let me go!

159
00:10:55,150 --> 00:10:57,352
-Oh no. -What are you doing?

160
00:11:02,023 --> 00:11:07,829
Which one's yours? The shabby gateball, or the ball signed by Shigeo Nagashima?

161
00:11:08,630 --> 00:11:10,098
The one signed by Nagashima.

162
00:11:10,332 --> 00:11:12,534
You liar! It was clearly the gateball!

163
00:11:13,101 --> 00:11:14,536
Let me borrow your fire.

164
00:11:18,039 --> 00:11:22,010
Damn it! How do they always know where I'm going?

165
00:11:22,210 --> 00:11:22,844
Huh?

166
00:11:25,347 --> 00:11:27,015
What's this cord?

167
00:11:28,883 --> 00:11:31,286
A battery in my handcuff case?

168
00:11:31,653 --> 00:11:32,354
Oh!

169
00:11:32,554 --> 00:11:35,357
They've been monitoring me with a navigation system!

170
00:11:35,924 --> 00:11:37,392
They thought of everything.

171
00:11:37,592 --> 00:11:39,895
But they won't catch me with this.

172
00:11:40,095 --> 00:11:43,565
I have an important mission to transfer money at the bank today

173
00:11:43,765 --> 00:11:48,370
so that my radio-controlled shuttle order doesn't get canceled.

174
00:11:48,570 --> 00:11:51,306
-Caw-ard! Caw-ard! -Who you callin' a coward?

175
00:11:51,539 --> 00:11:53,608
Caw-ard! Caw-ard!

176
00:11:53,842 --> 00:11:55,310
I've got it!

177
00:12:02,450 --> 00:12:07,389
My Ryo Navi isn't so delicate as to break just from him jumping into a river.

178
00:12:07,589 --> 00:12:10,892
Are you sure this thing is showing Ryo-san's location?

179
00:12:11,092 --> 00:12:13,228
I don't trust it.

180
00:12:13,428 --> 00:12:14,095
Huh?

181
00:12:15,063 --> 00:12:17,098
-Hey! -Oh, Ohara-san!

182
00:12:17,599 --> 00:12:19,901
How's it going? Have you caught Ryotsu?

183
00:12:20,101 --> 00:12:21,603
It's just a matter of time.

184
00:12:21,803 --> 00:12:24,406
But it's all thanks to your help.

185
00:12:24,606 --> 00:12:27,609
It was a piece of cake to switch Ryotsu's belt.

186
00:12:27,809 --> 00:12:29,778
"KAMEARI PARK POLICE STATION"

187
00:12:41,156 --> 00:12:45,593
I can't let him go on causing trouble for you all.

188
00:12:45,794 --> 00:12:48,897
Well, you can rest easy now. Leave it to us.

189
00:12:49,097 --> 00:12:50,131
Thank you.

190
00:12:50,332 --> 00:12:51,199
Ozaki-san!

191
00:12:51,566 --> 00:12:52,734
What is it?

192
00:12:52,934 --> 00:12:55,337
It suddenly stopped moving.

193
00:12:55,570 --> 00:12:56,972
Surely it's broken?

194
00:12:57,172 --> 00:12:59,007
That's impossible.

195
00:13:01,276 --> 00:13:02,110
We've got him!

196
00:13:02,310 --> 00:13:04,913
He's taking a rest after all that running away.

197
00:13:05,447 --> 00:13:08,216
Ohara-san. This will be it for Ryo-san.

198
00:13:08,450 --> 00:13:09,751
Oh, is it finally time?

199
00:13:09,951 --> 00:13:11,119
Come on, get in!

200
00:13:11,319 --> 00:13:12,120
Okay!

201
00:13:16,925 --> 00:13:18,927
Attention all personnel!

202
00:13:19,361 --> 00:13:22,197
&lt;i&gt;Ryo-san is holed up at the Kameari Hybrid Hotel.&lt;/i&gt;

203
00:13:22,764 --> 00:13:24,032
&lt;i&gt;That's where we end it.&lt;/i&gt;

204
00:13:24,833 --> 00:13:28,336
&lt;i&gt;Operation Sky Eye is entering its final stage.&lt;/i&gt;

205
00:13:28,536 --> 00:13:30,772
&lt;i&gt;All personnel head for the hotel!&lt;/i&gt;

206
00:13:35,810 --> 00:13:37,145
This way!

207
00:13:38,546 --> 00:13:39,681
Charge!

208
00:13:40,682 --> 00:13:42,851
Are you sure Ryo-san is in there?

209
00:13:43,051 --> 00:13:44,853
Just trust the technology, okay?

210
00:13:48,356 --> 00:13:52,026
This optional CD-ROM is synced up with the satellite's radio waves.

211
00:13:52,427 --> 00:13:56,231
It'll pinpoint Ryo-san's location in the hotel in the blink of an eye.

212
00:13:58,333 --> 00:13:59,734
This is the room.

213
00:14:00,101 --> 00:14:01,102
Attention everyone!

214
00:14:01,336 --> 00:14:04,072
Ryo-san is on the balcony of room 817.

215
00:14:04,272 --> 00:14:07,175
Team A, approach from room 816's balcony.

216
00:14:08,410 --> 00:14:10,745
&lt;i&gt;Team B, approach from room 818's balcony.&lt;/i&gt;

217
00:14:11,246 --> 00:14:15,383
&lt;i&gt;Teams C and D, enter room 817 directly.&lt;/i&gt;

218
00:14:17,051 --> 00:14:20,221
This will be make or break for Kameari Shopping District.

219
00:14:20,422 --> 00:14:23,391
Brace yourselves, everyone. And be sure to capture him!

220
00:14:23,758 --> 00:14:25,860
Yuki, we're finally alone.

221
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:27,228
Susumu-san...

222
00:14:30,865 --> 00:14:31,666
Shh!

223
00:14:37,705 --> 00:14:39,107
Team A is in position.

224
00:14:39,607 --> 00:14:40,675
&lt;i&gt;Team B, go ahead.&lt;/i&gt;

225
00:14:40,875 --> 00:14:44,612
Team B is in position on the balcony of room 818.

226
00:14:45,213 --> 00:14:46,314
&lt;i&gt;Teams C and D?&lt;/i&gt;

227
00:14:46,548 --> 00:14:48,850
Teams C and D are also in position.

228
00:14:49,050 --> 00:14:50,084
&lt;i&gt;Understood.&lt;/i&gt;

229
00:14:50,718 --> 00:14:52,087
Beginning the countdown.

230
00:14:52,487 --> 00:14:58,259
&lt;i&gt;Five, four, three, two, one...&lt;/i&gt;

231
00:14:58,460 --> 00:14:59,761
Attack!

232
00:15:08,636 --> 00:15:11,172
Status report. Did you capture the target?

233
00:15:11,406 --> 00:15:13,475
&lt;i&gt;-It's a crow!&lt;/i&gt; -A crow?

234
00:15:16,478 --> 00:15:20,415
It wasn't Ryo-san on the balcony. It was a crow wearing his belt!

235
00:15:21,883 --> 00:15:23,585
Th-That can't be!

236
00:15:23,785 --> 00:15:26,354
How could Operation Sky Eye fail?

237
00:15:28,490 --> 00:15:31,659
I told you. You can't trust technology.

238
00:15:34,496 --> 00:15:36,364
I've won again this year.

239
00:15:38,366 --> 00:15:41,369
"BOKUTO DAIICHI BANK"

240
00:15:42,003 --> 00:15:45,006
Now then. Time to make the payment.

241
00:15:45,206 --> 00:15:47,942
Oh, someone dropped some money.

242
00:15:48,142 --> 00:15:49,277
Money?

243
00:15:50,478 --> 00:15:52,380
Money! Money! Money!

244
00:15:53,448 --> 00:15:56,518
Oh, I found it. It's mine!

245
00:15:56,751 --> 00:15:57,352
Huh?

246
00:15:58,186 --> 00:15:59,154
"Toy bank"?

247
00:16:02,524 --> 00:16:04,959
Damn it! You tricked me, you cowards!

248
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:08,863
See? I caught him easily without any high-tech nonsense.

249
00:16:09,097 --> 00:16:12,033
I suppose this is the best method for catching Ryo-san.

250
00:16:12,233 --> 00:16:14,636
-Your experience paid off. -He's so pathetic.

251
00:16:14,836 --> 00:16:17,639
All my hard work up until now...

252
00:16:17,839 --> 00:16:20,842
It was for nothing!

253
00:16:22,043 --> 00:16:24,212
Come now, everyone. Get in line.

254
00:16:24,412 --> 00:16:26,648
May we begin, Ohara-san?

255
00:16:26,848 --> 00:16:29,250
Go ahead. Take it.

256
00:16:29,484 --> 00:16:31,386
Sorry, Ryo-san. It's ours now.

257
00:16:32,420 --> 00:16:34,856
What's wrong? You look awfully serious.

258
00:16:35,056 --> 00:16:37,659
No, it's my fault for not paying my debts.

259
00:16:37,859 --> 00:16:39,160
Go on, take it.

260
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:42,897
You sure? It's a bit disconcerting hearing you say it so simply.

261
00:16:43,131 --> 00:16:44,399
I'm sorry, Sachiko!

262
00:16:44,899 --> 00:16:48,503
It looks like it'll be a while before I can come and get you.

263
00:16:48,970 --> 00:16:51,506
-Who's that girl? -My little sister, Sachiko.

264
00:16:51,906 --> 00:16:54,709
She's working up north in a place so cold

265
00:16:54,909 --> 00:16:57,512
her hands and feet go numb and her bones freeze.

266
00:16:57,712 --> 00:16:58,413
What?

267
00:16:58,613 --> 00:17:02,083
A child? Working? How could that be?

268
00:17:04,252 --> 00:17:07,288
&lt;i&gt;It's a long story that I'll never forget.&lt;/i&gt;

269
00:17:07,522 --> 00:17:11,426
&lt;i&gt;Sachiko was born on a cold, snowy night.&lt;/i&gt;

270
00:17:12,727 --> 00:17:15,063
&lt;i&gt;Mom and Dad were overjoyed.&lt;/i&gt;

271
00:17:15,263 --> 00:17:20,268
&lt;i&gt;They named her Sachiko, hoping it would bring her happiness.&lt;/i&gt;

272
00:17:20,468 --> 00:17:21,436
&lt;i&gt;But...&lt;/i&gt;

273
00:17:31,546 --> 00:17:33,548
&lt;i&gt;Our parents died in a freak accident.&lt;/i&gt;

274
00:17:33,748 --> 00:17:36,284
&lt;i&gt;We were meant to receive some insurance money,&lt;/i&gt;

275
00:17:36,484 --> 00:17:39,287
&lt;i&gt;but we got swindled by a shady broker.&lt;/i&gt;

276
00:17:42,323 --> 00:17:46,094
To make matters worse, our house collapsed.

277
00:17:47,495 --> 00:17:53,034
And it turned out that our parents owed 200 million yen from a failed business.

278
00:17:53,234 --> 00:17:57,605
A relative took on the debt, but also took Sachiko with him.

279
00:17:57,805 --> 00:17:58,973
And then...

280
00:17:59,607 --> 00:18:03,478
&lt;i&gt;It turns out the relative runs a shady construction company.&lt;/i&gt;

281
00:18:03,678 --> 00:18:06,514
&lt;i&gt;He forces young Sachiko to work for him,&lt;/i&gt;

282
00:18:06,748 --> 00:18:08,983
&lt;i&gt;and he doesn't even feed her right.&lt;/i&gt;

283
00:18:09,450 --> 00:18:14,288
&lt;i&gt;Every time I try to get her back, he shows me the 200 million yen IOU.&lt;/i&gt;

284
00:18:14,489 --> 00:18:16,491
&lt;i&gt;And so I made a vow to myself.&lt;/i&gt;

285
00:18:16,991 --> 00:18:21,929
&lt;i&gt;It would be impossible to put in the hours to pay off the debt before she hits 20,&lt;/i&gt;

286
00:18:22,630 --> 00:18:26,768
&lt;i&gt;and so I put all of my salary and bonuses toward paying off the debt.&lt;/i&gt;

287
00:18:27,468 --> 00:18:31,706
&lt;i&gt;I knew the world would hate me for it, but I didn't care!&lt;/i&gt;

288
00:18:35,543 --> 00:18:37,712
But I was wrong, Sachiko.

289
00:18:38,112 --> 00:18:40,348
No matter how miserable you are,

290
00:18:40,548 --> 00:18:43,785
I shouldn't be troubling and relying on others so much.

291
00:18:43,985 --> 00:18:47,655
I'm a disgrace to humanity!

292
00:18:49,090 --> 00:18:51,292
So that's it... That's the truth...

293
00:18:51,659 --> 00:18:55,697
Please forgive my ignorance for calling you a piece of human trash.

294
00:18:55,930 --> 00:18:57,498
It's okay, Chief.

295
00:18:57,932 --> 00:19:00,968
Ryotsu may have been wrong in how he went about it,

296
00:19:01,402 --> 00:19:05,973
but he was trying to live an honorable life in his own way.

297
00:19:06,708 --> 00:19:10,978
For my sake, please forgive him.

298
00:19:11,412 --> 00:19:13,281
We're the ones in the wrong here.

299
00:19:13,481 --> 00:19:17,819
We tried to take Ryo-san's bonus without even considering his situation.

300
00:19:18,019 --> 00:19:20,722
Here's your bonus, Ryo-san.

301
00:19:20,955 --> 00:19:22,724
Go and give it to your sister.

302
00:19:23,157 --> 00:19:25,226
But this...

303
00:19:27,695 --> 00:19:30,364
Your debts can wait for as long as necessary.

304
00:19:30,565 --> 00:19:34,569
Compared to your situation, I'm a million times better off!

305
00:19:34,769 --> 00:19:36,237
Ryo-san, hang in there!

306
00:19:36,437 --> 00:19:37,538
Don't give up!

307
00:19:38,573 --> 00:19:41,075
I'll never forget your kindness!

308
00:19:41,309 --> 00:19:44,245
I'm sure my sister will be happy too!

309
00:19:49,083 --> 00:19:51,586
Hi, everyone. What brings you all here together?

310
00:19:51,786 --> 00:19:53,688
Oh, what's this?

311
00:19:53,888 --> 00:19:56,224
That's Ryotsu's sister, Sachiko.

312
00:19:56,424 --> 00:19:57,558
That's strange.

313
00:19:57,759 --> 00:19:59,560
-This is a magazine cutting. -Huh?

314
00:19:59,761 --> 00:20:02,730
And I don't think Ryotsu has a younger sister.

315
00:20:02,930 --> 00:20:04,465
What?

316
00:20:06,868 --> 00:20:12,006
Any fool who falls for a story like that isn't fit to steal my bonus.

317
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:13,908
Thank you very much.

318
00:20:14,108 --> 00:20:16,277
Now all that's left is to go to the bank.

319
00:20:20,448 --> 00:20:22,116
Argh! What the heck is this?

320
00:20:24,719 --> 00:20:26,621
Who did this to me?

321
00:20:26,821 --> 00:20:30,758
Based on previous data,

322
00:20:30,958 --> 00:20:34,629
there was a 95% chance you would make a stop at this café after shaking us.

323
00:20:36,798 --> 00:20:39,967
Just as I thought. It was worth the wait.

324
00:20:40,401 --> 00:20:42,637
The owner of the models shop! What is that?

325
00:20:42,904 --> 00:20:45,907
This is a weapon designed to collect debts from you.

326
00:20:46,107 --> 00:20:47,441
The Debt Shucker X!

327
00:20:47,775 --> 00:20:49,577
Debt Shucker X?

328
00:20:49,777 --> 00:20:53,114
I've been developing it in secret for next year's Bonus Battle.

329
00:20:53,314 --> 00:20:55,450
It's already 80% complete.

330
00:20:55,917 --> 00:20:59,454
According to my calculations, this should be enough to defeat you.

331
00:21:04,459 --> 00:21:06,460
Your calculations are way off!

332
00:21:06,961 --> 00:21:10,598
Only Ryo-san could engage in a tug-of-war with this Debt Shucker X!

333
00:21:17,271 --> 00:21:18,606
He's holding out!

334
00:21:22,109 --> 00:21:24,412
We can't have that. Electric shock!

335
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:33,888
You trying to kill me?!

336
00:21:34,455 --> 00:21:35,656
Rest assured.

337
00:21:35,857 --> 00:21:40,461
The voltage is not enough to kill a normal man, much less you, Ryotsu.

338
00:21:40,661 --> 00:21:43,197
But, it should be enough to knock you out!

339
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,802
Electric shock!

340
00:21:50,171 --> 00:21:51,205
Shock!

341
00:21:55,476 --> 00:21:56,477
My bonus...

342
00:21:57,512 --> 00:21:59,981
It pains me to be so rough with you,

343
00:22:00,314 --> 00:22:03,284
but it's your own fault for not paying your debts.

344
00:22:03,484 --> 00:22:05,586
And now for that bonus...

345
00:22:06,587 --> 00:22:08,289
Huh?

346
00:22:08,756 --> 00:22:10,191
What's wrong?

347
00:22:14,395 --> 00:22:16,163
I'm so close!

348
00:22:23,170 --> 00:22:25,072
Damn it!

349
00:22:25,306 --> 00:22:29,343
Now do you see? You want to take my bonus? Impossible!

350
00:22:30,177 --> 00:22:34,348
The chief may say you can, but God says you can't!

351
00:22:39,153 --> 00:22:41,088
Even God...

352
00:22:41,322 --> 00:22:44,258
Hold it! Get back here!

353
00:22:44,926 --> 00:22:46,527
Stay away from me!

354
00:22:46,727 --> 00:22:48,095
Pay your debts!

355
00:22:48,329 --> 00:22:50,431
Stop! What are you doing?

356
00:22:56,170 --> 00:22:57,071
Watch it!

357
00:23:06,414 --> 00:23:08,749
What is Ryotsu doing?

358
00:23:16,257 --> 00:23:20,995
Banks will exchange damaged banknotes if they retain their original form.

359
00:23:21,228 --> 00:23:23,230
This is painful to watch.

360
00:23:23,431 --> 00:23:27,635
I'll help you, Ryotsu, but only if you use it to pay your debts.

361
00:23:27,835 --> 00:23:29,236
Don't talk to me!

362
00:23:29,437 --> 00:23:32,073
I need to concentrate!

363
00:23:32,840 --> 00:23:33,641
Hmph!

364
00:23:35,943 --> 00:23:37,578
Oh no!

365
00:23:37,778 --> 00:23:40,014
My bonus!

366
00:23:46,253 --> 00:23:51,692
I'll get my hands on your next bonus for sure, Kankichi Ryotsu!

367
00:23:54,228 --> 00:23:57,031
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

368
00:23:57,264 --> 00:24:02,637
THE DEBT SHUCKER X AND MUCH, MUCH MORE
